<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zanata Berbers</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zanata</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zanata were one of the major <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> confederations of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>, many of them pastoral nomads of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maghreb">Maghreb</a> and the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>. They played a large role in the politics of the medieval Maghreb, later founding the Marinid and Zayyanid dynasties. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana-empire">Ghana Empire</a> record that Ghana captured the trans-Saharan oasis city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awdaghast">Awdaghast</a> from Zanata Berbers in 992 CE.</p></div>
